hadiths[25]{hadithnumber,text}:
"274","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both) picked up a date from the dates of charity and put it in his mouth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: ""Do not take it, do not take it."" So he spat it out. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not know that charity is not lawful for us?"
"275","Muhammad bin Ziyad narrated: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate: Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with both of them) took (a date), then he mentioned as in the previous hadith."
"276","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: Dates of charity were presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace be upon him) lifted Hasan or Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) onto his shoulder, and their saliva began to flow. He saw that there was a date from the charity dates in their mouth. So he shook them, and they spat it out. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not know, charity is not lawful for us."
"277","Narrated with the same chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One who exceeds the limits in charity is like the one who withholds it."
"278","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When food from someone’s house was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he would ask about it. If it was said that it was a gift, he would eat from it, and if it was said that it was charity, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: “Eat,” and he would not eat from it."
"279","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The needy is not the one who goes door to door for a morsel or two, or a date or two; rather, the needy is the one who does not possess enough wealth to make him independent, and he does not cling to people asking them, or he feels shy to cling to people and ask from them."
"280","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The needy is not the one..."" Then the narrator reported the hadith similar to the previous one: The narrator said that Shu’bah was uncertain about one date or two dates."
"281","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not like that I should have gold equal to the mountain of Uhud and then three days pass while even a single dinar from it remains with me, except that which I keep for the repayment of a debt."
"282","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! How should I give charity?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you are healthy and stingy, hoping for life and fearing poverty, and do not delay to the extent that when your soul reaches your throat, you say: My wealth is for so-and-so and for so-and-so, for it has already become theirs."
"283","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: Wealth is not the abundance of possessions, but true wealth is the richness of the heart."
"284","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Abundance of wealth and possessions is not richness, but richness of the heart is the real richness."
"285","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The one who gives charity does not receive more reward than the needy person who takes charity."
"286","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until wealth becomes so abundant and there is such an overflow of wealth that a wealthy person will be concerned about who will accept his charity; he will offer it, but the person to whom he offers it will say: (Sir) I have no need of it."
"287","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""I see a fallen date and pick it up with the intention of eating it, but then, fearing that it might be from charity, I throw it away."
"288","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I came with my maternal aunt, who was a newlywed bride, to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) so that we could pledge allegiance to you. You saw that she was wearing two gold bangles and rings, so you said to her: ""Do you like that Allah should make you wear bracelets of fire and brand you with rings of fire?"" So she immediately took them off and threw them away; it is not known who picked them up. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Could not one of you make two silver earrings and then color them with ambergris, wars, or saffron?"
"289","Lady Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us one day while the color of his face had changed. I realized that something was troubling him. I said: O Messenger of Allah! What is the reason that I see the color of your face has changed? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Are you not aware of those nine dinars that came to us yesterday, and the night passed while we had not spent them?”"
"290","Lady Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us to give charity, so Abdullah (bin Mas'ud’s, may Allah be pleased with him) wife Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with charity and said: O Messenger of Allah! Abdullah has little wealth and I have orphaned nephews, so if I spend on them from charity, will it suffice on my behalf, while I spend on them from such and such sources, and in every situation (I spend on them)? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Yes.” The narrator stated, she was a craftswoman."
"291","It is narrated from Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: O Messenger of Allah! The children of Abu Salamah are under my care (guardianship), is it sufficient for me to spend on them from charity, and I do not let any opportunity to spend on them slip by? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes."
"292","Zainab Thaqafiyyah narrated: I used to save my wealth, so I said: I will keep it in the best place with me. I said in my heart: If I spend it in the way of Allah on any army of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) that you send, or if I buy a Muslim slave girl and set her free, or give it in charity to the poor, or give it in charity to my husband who has little wealth, or give it in charity to my orphan nephews under my care. So I came to Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) to ask her about this. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came and said: ""Aisha! Who is this?"" She replied: The wife of Ibn Umm Abd. He said: ""Why has she come?"" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned this to him, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""She should spend it on her husband who has little wealth and on her orphan nephews under her care; for her there will be double reward."
"293","Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: The wife of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) was skilled; she used to make things and then sell them. Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) and his children did not have wealth. His wife said to him: ""You have distracted me from giving charity."" So Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""If there is no reward for you in (spending) on us, then I do not like that you do this."" So she went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and related the whole incident to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will have a reward for whatever you spend on them, so spend on them."
"294","It is narrated from Sha'bi (may Allah have mercy on him) that the wife of Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her), asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about the issue of giving charity to relatives. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Giving charity to relatives earns double the reward compared to giving charity to non-relatives."
"295","Ibrahim (Nakhai, may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: The wife of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have jewelry and my orphan nephews are under my care, so can I spend the zakat of my jewelry on them? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes."
"296","Ibrahim (Nakhai, may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: The wife of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: The nephews of mine or of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with her) are under my care; can I spend my zakat on them from my wealth? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes."
"297","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: The wife of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: The nephews of Abdullah are under my care. If I spend charity from my wealth on them, will that suffice for me? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes."
"298","The wife of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her), narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to us and encouraged us to give charity. He said: “O group of women, give charity, even if it is from your jewelry, for on the Day of Resurrection, the majority of the inhabitants of Hell will be from among you.” She narrated: Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) had little wealth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was a person of awe-inspiring presence. I said to Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about giving charity to our husbands and to the orphan children under our care. He said: No, rather you yourself ask the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). So I went to the door and saw a woman from the Ansar there; she had the same issue as I did. Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us, so we said to him: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for us whether giving charity to our husbands and to the orphan children under our care will suffice for us. Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) went inside, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Who is at the door?” He replied: Zainab, the wife of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), and another woman; they are asking you about an issue: Will giving charity to their husbands and to the orphan children under their care suffice for them? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “For both of them, there is a double reward for giving charity and for maintaining kinship ties.”"
